PROPERTY  KINDEX  
#Tail is a result of the calibration with (./QuantumEfficiencyTester -precision 0.01 -cal) starting from extrapolation of "motta_KINDEX" value
#Note that THREESTEPPROBABILITY tails should first be defined from the fit of the QEmeas/QEcalc
#Also Glass properties are not known below 340nm. So First the glass was adjusted by hand to have a smoother shape going to UV region (looking also at Japanese Degg glass).
# UNITS  nm\E 1
OPTION wavelength
#280 1.83
#290 1.96
#310 1.94
#330 1.87
#340 1.8
#360 1.85
#370 1.74
#In the new approach (glass absorption is removed from QE before the QE tuning, it is not clear how to tune K & Glass absroption below 380. Curves from Murtaza et al and Motta does not allow some obvious extrapolation (they differ quite a lot0. So it was decided to keep K constant below 380 nm.
280 1.95
310 1.57
320 1.69
350 1.8
